    "/v1/fetch_rate_plans": {
      "get": {
        "summary": "Fetch rate plan adjustments for your listings",
        "description": "If your listings have rate plan adjusments, then you can use this API call to fetch those adjustments. You can fetch the prices for the default rate plan using the /listing_prices call and use the adjustments returned in this call to derive the prices of the non-default rate plans for your system.",
        "operationId": "fetchRatePlans",
        "tags": [
          "Prices"
        ],
        "parameters": [
          {
            "name": "X-API-Key",
            "in": "header",
            "schema": {
              "type": "string",
              "example": "{{API_KEY}}"
            }
          },
          {
            "name": "listing_id",
            "in": "query",
            "schema": {
              "type": "string",
              "example": "{{listing_id}}"
            }
          },
          {
            "name": "pms_name",
            "in": "query",
            "schema": {
              "type": "string",
              "example": "{{pms_name}}"
            }
          }
        ],
        "responses": {
          "200": {
            "description": "Success",
            "content": {
              "application/json": {
                "schema": {
                  "type": "array",
                  "items": {
                    "type": "object",
                    "properties": {
                      "rate_plans": {
                        "type": "object",
                        "properties": {
                          "id": {
                            "type": "string"
                          },
                          "pms": {
                            "type": "string"
                          },
                          "name": {
                            "type": "string"
                          },
                          "rateplans": {
                            "type": "object",
                            "properties": {
                              "rate_plan_id": {
                                "type": "object",
                                "properties": {
                                  "name": {
                                    "type": "string"
                                  },
                                  "type": {
                                    "type": "string"
                                  },
                                  "default": {
                                    "type": "string"
                                  },
                                  "plan_type": {
                                    "type": "string"
                                  },
                                  "adjustment": {
                                    "type": "number"
                                  },
                                  "update_type": {
                                    "type": "string"
                                  }
                                }
                              }
                            }
                          }
                        }
                      }
                    }
                  }
                }
              }
            }
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "/v1/neighborhood_data": {
      "get": {
        "summary": "Get neighborhood data for a listing",
        "tags": [
          "Neighborhood Data"
        ],
        "description": "Get neighborhood data for your listing with all stats that show up in the \"Neighborhood Tab\". \nThe data returned by this API call will majorly contain:\n\n  1. Total number of listings considered in this neighborhood.\n\n  2. Basic listing information including currency, latitude and longitude of the listing.\n\n  3. Source of the data: The source of data will be Airbnb or VRBO as indicated in the response.\n\n  4. Future Percentile Prices for the listing: For each bedroom category identified by the key, we return a different percentile price for the market for each stay date. In order to comprehend this data, it is important to note that there are 4 key pieces of information in the response:\n  \n          Key\n          X_values\n          Y_values\n          Labels\n    \n    \n          Key details:\n          -1: \"Room\"\n          0: \"Studio\"\n          1: \"1BR\" and so on.\n          \n          \n      X_values contain an array of future dates Labels:\n      For \"Future Percentile Prices,\" these will be the 25th Percentile, 50th Percentile, 75th Percentile, Median Booked Price, 90th Percentile. \n      \n      Y_values: There are 5 corresponding arrays in Y_values. These 5 arrays in Y_values denote the data for the labels mentioned in the \"Labels\" array for each date in X_values.\n      \n      In the example given in the success response below, we have provided a compact response for 3 future dates. \n      \n      For Category 0 (Studio), the 25th Percentile value of the Future Percentile Price for 2023-11-15 is 92.7. Similarly, the 50th Percentile value of Future Percentile Price for 2023-11-15 is 115.1.\n  \n  \n5. Future Occ/New/Canc: For each bedroom category identified by the key, we provide occupancy and pickup for the future, as well as occupancy, pickup, and final occupancy from the same time last year. Similar to 'Future Percentile Prices,' labels are present in the API response for the identification of different arrays.\nThe response structure is the same as in Future Percentile Prices. Labels for Future Occ/New/Canc Response are as follows:\n\n        Occupancy\n        New Bookings\n        Canceled Bookings\n        Occupancy_LY\n        Occupancy_STLY\n        New_Bookings_STLY\n        \n    In the example mentioned, the label 'Occupancy' for category 0 on 2023-05-19 is 87.5. Similarly, 'New Bookings' for category 0 on 2023-05-19 is 0. The value of Occupancy_LY (final occupancy last year) for 2023-05-19 is 91.1765.\n\n\n  6. Summary Table Base Price: For each bedroom category identified by the key, we provide different percentile prices considering the past 180 and future 180 days.\n  \n      API Response structure is the same as in Future Percentile Prices. Labels for Summary Table Base Price Response are as follows:\n  \n          25th Percentile Price\n          50th Percentile Price\n          75th Percentile Price\n          90th Percentile Price\n          \n      If the ND source is a Market Dashboard, then following additional Labels will be provided:\n      \n          Median Listed Price (USD)\n          Median Booked Nightly Price (USD)\n          Median Booked Weekly Price (USD)\n          Median Booked Monthly Price (USD)\n          Median LOS\n          Median Lead Time\n          \n      The Summary Table Base Price for the same category 0 can also be identified. The 25th Percentile Price of 'Summary Table Base Price' is 98. The '50th Percentile Price' of the Base price for category 0 is 126.\n      \n  About Market KPI:\n  \n  The market KPI JSON object stores aggregated data at a monthly level, along with data for the last 365 days and the last 730 days. It has two main keys: Category and Labels.\n  \n    1. Category:\n          a. This key contains sub-keys where each sub-key represents a specific bedroom type (e.g., 1 Bedroom, 2 Bedroom, etc.).\n          \n          b. Each bedroom type contains a data object with two keys:\n          \n              i. X_values: A 1-dimensional array that represents the time periods for which data is available.\n              \n              ii. Y_values: A 2-dimensional array with 5 rows, where each row corresponds to a specific KPI (Key Performance Indicator).\n              \n          c. The number of columns in Y_values matches the number of elements in X_values, indicating KPI values for the periods specified in X_values.\n          \n    2. Labels:\n      a. This key provides the names of the KPIs corresponding to the rows in Y_values. (value of this will be a  [\"Total Available Days\",\"Booking Window\",\"LOS\",\"Revenue\",\"Total Booked Days\"] )\n      \n    KPI Details :\n    \n      Total Available Days : This represents the total number of days that all the listings in the area were available for booking during the specified period.\n      \n      Booking Window : This shows you the median number of days between when the date the booking was made and the first stay date for that booking during the specific period.\n      \n      LOS : This shows how many nights a clients are booking the properties per reservation during that specific period.\n      Revenue : This is the total revenue generated from bookings across all listings in the area during the period.\n      \n      Total Booked Days : This KPI reflects the total number of days that were booked across all listings in the area during the period.\n    ",
        "operationId": "getNeighborhoodDataForAListing",
        "parameters": [
          {
            "name": "pms",
            "in": "query",
            "required": true,
            "schema": {
              "type": "string",
